AC|ANTENNA TUNER|ACP1P2P3;|AC;|P1 RX AT 0 OFF 1 ON (ignored in Set, enter 1); P2 TX AT 0 OFF 1 ON; P3 0 stop tuning / inactive; 1 start tuning / active. Start tuning with AC111;
AG|AF LEVEL|AGP1P1P1;|AG;|P1 000-255
AI|AUTO INFORMATION|AIP1;|AI;|P1 0 OFF; 2 ON (not backed up); 4 ON (backed up); 1 and 3 not used. Set separately for USB, COM and LAN connectors
AM|AUTO MODE|AMP1;|AM;|P1 0 OFF; 1 ON
AN|ANTENNA SELECTION|ANP1P2P3P4;|AN;|P1 1 ANT1 2 ANT2 9 no change; P2 RX ANT used 0/1 9 no change; P3 drive out 0/1 9 no change; P4 antenna output for ext receiver 0/1 9 no change (9 set only)
AP0|AUDIO PEAK FILTER ON/OFF|AP0P1;|AP0;|P1 1 APF OFF; 2 APF ON
AP1|AUDIO PEAK FILTER SHIFT|AP1P1P1;|AP1;|P1 00-80 (40 center, 5 Hz steps, 00=-200 Hz, 80=+200 Hz); 99 initial value (set only)
AP2|AUDIO PEAK FILTER BANDWIDTH|AP2P1;|AP2;|P1 0 NAR; 1 MID; 2 WIDE; 9 initial (set only)
AP3|AUDIO PEAK FILTER GAIN|AP3P1;|AP3;|P1 0-6; 9 initial (set only)
AQ0|AGC QUICK RECOVERY ON/OFF|AQ0P1;|AQ0;|P1 1 OFF; 2 ON; not usable in FM
AQ1|AGC QUICK RECOVERY THRESHOLD|AQ1P1P1;|AQ1;|P1 01-10; 99 initial (set only); not usable in FM
AS0|AUTO MODE FREQUENCY DIVISION REGISTER|AS0P1(11)P2;||P1 upper limit frequency Hz 11 digits; P2 mode (OM P2 codes); max 32 divisions
AS1|NUMBER OF AUTO MODE DIVISIONS||AS1;|Answer AS1P1P1; P1 00-32
AS2|AUTO MODE DIVISION READOUT||AS2P1P1;|P1 00-31; answer AS2P1P1P2(11)P3; P2 upper limit Hz; P3 mode
AS3|DELETE AUTO MODE DIVISION|AS3P1P1;||P1 00-31
BC|BEAT CANCEL|BCP1;|BC;|P1 0 OFF; 1 BC1; 2 BC2
BD|BAND DOWN / BAND SELECT|BDP1P2P2;|BD;|Setting 1: BDP1P2P2; (P1 VFO ignored, P2 band 00 1.8M 01 3.5M 02 7M 03 10M 04 14M 05 18M 06 21M 07 24M 08 28M 09 50M 10 GENE); Setting 2: BD; = [DOWN]; answer BDP1P3; P3 band memory 0-3
BU|BAND UP|BU;|BU;|Same as BD: BU; = [UP]; setting 1 BUP1P2P2;; AI response uses BU;
BI|BREAK-IN|BIP1;|BI;|P1 0 OFF; 1 ON; settable in CW only, reads 0 in other modes
BK|BLANKING OF RECEIVED SIGNAL|BKP1;|BK;|P1 0 OFF; 1 ON; not backed up
BP|NOTCH FREQUENCY|BPP1P1P1;|BP;|P1 000-255
BS0|SCOPE DISPLAY ON/OFF|BS0P1;|BS0;|P1 0 OFF; 1 ON
